      "metadata.bejson",
      ".bejson",
      "{\n  \"Format\": \"BEJSON\",\n  \"Format_Version\": \"104\",\n  \"Format_Creator\": \"Elton Boehnen\",\n  \"Parent_Hierarchy\": \"../104a.mfdb.bejson\",\n  \"Records_Type\": [\n    \"Metadata\"\n  ],\n  \"Fields\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"RECORD_TYPE\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"LIBRARY_FAMILY\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"LANGUAGE\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"KEY\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"VALUE\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"DESCRIPTION\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"Values\": [\n    [\n      \"VERSION\",\n      \"ECOSYSTEM\",\n      \"ALL\",\n      \"CURRENT_VERSION\",\n      \"2.0.48\",\n      \"2026-08-26: Phase 6 TS port -- 105-series Referential Integrity in TypeScript (checkReferentialIntegrity standalone audit, checkFKWrite/checkEntityDroppable/resolveDeleteDependents enforcement helpers, advisory Ref_Integrity switch). TS is now fully caught up to Python's Phase 2/3/4/6/8 status. Two more pre-existing bugs found and flagged (not fixed, outside scope): registerEntity() crashes on omitted record_count (parseInt(null) coercion bug), and the fs/path/require Node-only functions bug flagged earlier this session.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"VERSION\",\n      \"Core\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"CURRENT_VERSION\",\n      \"2.5.0\",\n      \"2.5.0: Format 105 Integrity Era support added (bejson_core.py 3.0.0, bejson_validator.py 3.0.0, new bejson_upgrade.py 1.0.0). 104-series untouched.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"VERSION\",\n      \"Core\",\n      \"JS\",\n      \"CURRENT_VERSION\",\n      \"2.3.0\",\n      \"\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"VERSION\",\n      \"Core\",\n      \"TS\",\n      \"CURRENT_VERSION\",\n      \"2.2.0\",\n      \"2.2.0: Phase 6 Referential Integrity ported (mfdb_core.ts enforcement helpers + mfdb_validators.ts standalone audit). TS Core now at full parity with Python's Format 105 work (Phases 2/3/4/6/8).\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"VERSION\",\n      \"Core\",\n      \"SH\",\n      \"CURRENT_VERSION\",\n      \"1.4.0\",\n      \"\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"RULE\",\n      \"Core\",\n      \"ALL\",\n      \"LANGUAGE_PARITY_REQUIRED\",\n      \"true\",\n      \"Core is the only family required to be implemented in parity across all four language systems (PY/JS/TS/SH). Confirmed by Elton Boehnen, 2026-07-18.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"RULE\",\n      \"ALL\",\n      \"ALL\",\n      \"MFDB_IS_PART_OF_CORE\",\n      \"true\",\n      \"MFDB is implemented as part of the Core family, not a separate family directory or a family requiring its own errors file. Confirmed by Elton Boehnen, 2026-07-18.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"RULE\",\n      \"ALL\",\n      \"ALL\",\n      \"FAMILY_OWNS_ITS_ERROR_CODES\",\n      \"true\",\n      \"Each family maintains its own lib_bejson_<Family>_bejson_errors.<ext> file. Core must not hold error codes belonging to another family.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"RULE\",\n      \"ALL\",\n      \"ALL\",\n      \"BEJSON_ACRONYM_DEFINITION\",\n      \"BOEHNEN ELTON JSON\",\n      \"BEJSON stands for BOEHNEN ELTON JSON. This is the sole authoritative definition; no other expansion of the acronym is valid. Confirmed by Elton Boehnen, 2026-07-21. Also stated verbatim in the header of all four Core language files (PY/JS/TS/SH).\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}",
