      "schemas.bejson",
      ".bejson",
      "{\n  \"Format\": \"BEJSON\",\n  \"Format_Version\": \"104\",\n  \"Format_Creator\": \"Elton Boehnen\",\n  \"Parent_Hierarchy\": \"../104a.mfdb.bejson\",\n  \"Records_Type\": [\n    \"Schemas\"\n  ],\n  \"Fields\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"SCHEMA_NAME\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"OWNING_FAMILY\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"LANGUAGE\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"VERSION\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"FIELD_DEFINITIONS\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"DESCRIPTION\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"SOURCE_FILE\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"Values\": [\n    [\n      \"SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY\",\n      \"Core\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"5\",\n      \"[{\\\"name\\\": \\\"version\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"file_path\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"file_name\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"content\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"is_binary\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"is_base64\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"}]\",\n      \"MFDB Chunker v5 entity schema (6 fields: version/file_path/file_name/content/is_binary/is_base64). TRUE DUPLICATE resolved: diffed byte-for-byte identical field lists between Core.SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY_v5 and Utility.SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY - genuinely the same schema under two names in two files. Merged into this single DB row as the one source of truth.\",\n      \"Lib_PY/Core/lib_bejson_Core_bejson_schema.py (as SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY_v5); Lib_PY/Utility/lib_bejson_Utility_bejson_utility.py (as SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY)\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"SCHEMA_MFDB_MANIFEST_v5\",\n      \"Core\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"5\",\n      \"[{\\\"name\\\": \\\"entity_name\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"file_path\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"description\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"record_count\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"schema_version\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"primary_key\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"changelog\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"chunked_at\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"tags\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}]\",\n      \"MFDB Chunker v5 manifest schema (9 fields).\",\n      \"Lib_PY/Core/lib_bejson_Core_bejson_schema.py\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"SCHEMA_MODEL_REGISTRY__Core\",\n      \"Core\",\n      \"PY\",\n      \"2.1.2\",\n      \"{\\\"Records_Type\\\": [\\\"AI_Model\\\"], \\\"Fields\\\": [{\\\"name\\\": \\\"display_name\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"model_id\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"currently_active\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"thinking_enabled\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"google_search_enabled\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"}]}\",\n      \"AI_Model registry (Gemini models: display_name/model_id/currently_active/thinking_enabled/google_search_enabled). NAME COLLISION resolved, not a duplicate: diffed against AI.SCHEMA_MODEL_REGISTRY and confirmed they are genuinely different schemas (different Records_Type, different field sets, different model vendor) that happen to share the same Python constant name in two files. Kept as two separate DB rows, distinguished here by OWNING_FAMILY suffix in SCHEMA_NAME. Flagging for you: the identical constant name across Core and AI risks accidental shadowing/confusion at import time - candidate for a rename in a future confirmed pass (out of scope this turn, not touched).\",\n      \"Lib_PY/Core/lib_bejson_Core_bejson_schema.py\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}",
      "1.32",
      "4ed6cf47d7358c45d659b91258fe491e2bfb9dd9293ba8d9273471bbd0d3485c",
      "data/schemas.bejson",
      false,
      false
    ],
    [
      "DEPENDENCIES_ENTITY_USAGE.md",
      ".md",
      "# Dependencies Entity \u2014 Usage Note\n\nBefore deleting, moving, or renaming any library file, query the\n`Dependencies` entity (`data/dependencies.bejson`) for rows where\n`DEPENDS_ON_FILE` matches the file's path. Any match is a file that will\nbreak if the target is removed or moved without updating its import.\n\nComposite key: `FROM_LIBRARY_FAMILY + FROM_LANGUAGE + FROM_FILE + DEPENDS_ON_FILE`\n(no single `primary_key` \u2014 set to `null` in the manifest).\n\nScope of this pass: internal edges only \u2014 one library file importing\nanother library file. External/stdlib imports (`os`, `json`, `pathlib`,\n`fs`, `path`, third-party packages) are intentionally excluded; they were\ndetected as unresolved references during the scan and skipped by design,\nnot missed.\n",
      "1.32",
      "debb4b18d553469ea22828a1cdd2ad86b83d3b8557374b5efa3a85649e188a76",
      "docs/DEPENDENCIES_ENTITY_USAGE.md",
      false,
      false
    ],
    [
      "TEMPLATES_ENTITY_USAGE.md",
      ".md",
      "# Templates Entity \u2014 Usage Note\n\nBefore writing a new library file, family error-registry skeleton, or MFDB\nentity/manifest file, pull the matching row from the `Templates` entity\n(`data/templates.bejson`) instead of copying an example file by eye.\n\nQuery by `TEMPLATE_TYPE` (`file_header` / `new_family_errors` /\n`new_mfdb_entity` / `new_mfdb_manifest`) and `LANGUAGE` (`PY` / `JS` / `TS` /\n`SH` / `ALL`). `TEMPLATE_BODY` is the literal template text with placeholder\ntokens (`{LIBRARY_NAME}`, `{FAMILY}`, `{VERSION}`, `{DATE}`,\n`{RELATIONAL_ID}`, etc.) to substitute before writing the new file.\n\nNote: `JS_TS_File_Header` covers both JS and TS with `LANGUAGE = \"ALL\"` since\nthe header block is byte-identical in shape between the two languages.\n",
      "1.32",
      "b17d10548c26841bf5869724cc195b8b539ecfc3af25dccdec64cda124188484",
      "docs/TEMPLATES_ENTITY_USAGE.md",
      false,
      false
    ],
    [
      "SCHEMAS_ENTITY_MIGRATION_DECISION.md",
      ".md",
      "# Schemas Entity \u2014 Migration-Style Decision (Task 3, Open Question #1)\n\n**Decision (delegated to Claude by Elton, 2026-07-22):** the Schemas entity\nstarts as a **reference/audit mirror**, not the live source libraries load\nfrom at runtime. Library files keep their local SCHEMA_* constants as-is;\nnone were modified this pass.\n\n**Why, for the long run:** rewiring every consuming file across four\nlanguages to load schema definitions from the MFDB at import time is a\nlarge, cross-cutting change \u2014 it touches import logic in Core, AI, CMS, and\nUtility simultaneously. Elton's own standing policy calls for surgical,\none-goal-at-a-time changes confirmed before moving to the next, and for\nnever altering existing libraries without a verified bug + a documented\nexception. Doing the full rewrite in the same pass that just inventoried\nthe schemas would violate both.\n\nThe audit mirror still solves the actual problem stated in the plan\n(drifting duplicate copies) for the two cases found this pass:\n- `SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY_v5` / `SCHEMA_MFDB_ENTITY` were a **true duplicate**\n  (byte-identical field lists, diffed) \u2014 now merged into one DB row, so an\n  AI or human can name it as \"the\" schema instead of picking a copy.\n- `SCHEMA_MODEL_REGISTRY` in Core and AI is **not** a duplicate \u2014 diffed and\n  confirmed genuinely different schemas (Gemini AI_Model vs\n  OpenRouterModelRegistry) that happen to share a Python constant name.\n  Recorded as two distinct rows (`SCHEMA_MODEL_REGISTRY__Core` /\n  `SCHEMA_MODEL_REGISTRY__AI`); the name collision itself is flagged as a\n  candidate for a future rename, not something fixed in this pass.\n\n**Recommended next step (not started, needs its own confirmed task):**\nmigrate consuming files to load from the DB one family at a time, starting\nwith the Core/Utility MFDB_ENTITY merge since that pair is already unified\nin the DB and is the smallest, lowest-risk case.\n\n**SCHEMA_PROJECT_v140:** migrated into the DB as-is (not dropped) since PMS\nis being rebuilt from scratch and no replacement schema exists yet;\n`DESCRIPTION` notes it should not be used for new work until the PMS\nrebuild lands.\n",
      "1.32",
      "e624a06ceed927e9af3d83b178f2e84ec22f129d05425de9b2c9c7a866742e55",
      "docs/SCHEMAS_ENTITY_MIGRATION_DECISION.md",
      false,
      false
    ]
  ],
  "MFDB_Version": "1.32",
